{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/573406-how-big-are-your-packs-territories","id":573406,"title":"How big are your packs' territories?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-29T18:31:31-07:00","id":573406,"title":"How big are your packs' territories?","content":"When you're setting-building, how much territory do packs claim? If they're an urban pack? Rural?<br /> <br /> How much turf out there isn't claimed by any pack?<br /> <br /> I remember seeing a line that described a county as a very large amount of territory, yet if every pack in the USA claimed a county and half of the USA had no packs, that still makes for 1500 werewolf packs in the USA, which seems like a lot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T18:47:36-07:00","id":573433,"title":"","content":"There's probably a lot of unclaimed territory that werewolves nearby would assure you is 'claimed' by them. But it really depends on your game, and it <i>should </i>depend on your game.<br /> <br /> In my first game we were in New York, which was just crowded with werewolves, and we owned one side of a street for half a block, then after defeating a neighboring pack, the entire block. The game after that a quintet of werewolves claimed an entire town and its surrounding environs. In a later game the pack had several blocks worth of prime real estate territory in Miami Beach, but there weren't that many werewolves around. And in the game we're playing now we haven't technically claimed it but we're working on getting a large area under our control.<br /> <br /> Throughout the books there are packs that run entire towns and counties, lots of nomads, and even more unclaimed territory.<br /> <br /> Generally the idea is in the wilderness there's more land to spread out so everyone has larger territories compared to city wolves where wolves have less territory spread out territory but there's more ground to patrol with large buildings and shops and more things going on with all the activity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T22:34:20-07:00","id":573616,"title":"","content":"My first and only (so far) werewolf chronicle also took place in New York with the pack claiming Sunset Park and Greenwood cemetery (gotta have green space). As they grew stronger they spread into South Slope and are now making inroads into Queens. The size of their territory has been dictated by their ability to patrol it and has thus grown with them as they eliminate threats in expanding circles.<br /> My New York doesn't have that many packs, the players in Sunset, a more traditional gang structured pack in the Bronx, a lone wolf Iron Master in Battery Park (his pack minus two were all killed with the twin towers and he later became a bale wolf, covenanted with the spirit of Gluttony in exchange for the 'return' of his fellows), a large, wealthy and old pack with lots of wolf blooded in the Hamptons who claimed the waters of the Atlantic as their territory, and a group of Ivory Claws who had recently wiped out and replaced a pack on Staten Island.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T05:55:41-07:00","id":573829,"title":"","content":"Werewolves can claim as much territory as they can hold. If there's a high population density and lots of competition, the size will be small. If population density is low, then we're talking large territories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:37:04-07:00","id":573873,"title":"","content":"In our campaign (San Francisco Area), we initially started out with Alcatraz Island and the nearby piers as our territory (Our Totem was Feasting Shark - he was such an awesome totem, it was sad to see him go).<br /> <br /> Eventually we sacrificed Alcatraz Island and claimed Treasure Island. From there we extended to the Financial District and eventually to the Mission District.<br /> As the campaign progressed, we solidified the Mission District, and claimed Haight Ashbury and the Art District, as well as Chinatown, giving up Treasure Island as sort of a neutral ground for the packs in the city (there were about 5-6 Forsaken packs in the city, and a Pure Pack).<br /> <br /> In the end, due to story, we decided the other packs were sluffing their duties, so we claimed San Francisco City as a whole (there was this multi-sided Supernatural war going on at the time, and several of the packs were really new packs, with relatively new werewolves). Was a lot of work trying to control the entire city, but it sure was fun. Turned pretty dark there towards the end, but still a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-30-2015, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}